      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults is 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** A single dose of 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. They probably won't give more pain relief.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **800 mg by mouth, three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (the usual dose for pain or inflammation).\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you really want the dose as written, confirm that and tell me the clinical reason. I can add that to the order note, though I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
